# Cloudflare Pages redirects (Netlify uses the same file and syntax).
#
# Short links, so a URL can be pasted into a message or read out in a meeting
# without anyone mistyping "01-editorial-atelier".

/t1      /templates/01-editorial-atelier/        302
/t5      /templates/05-neighbourhood/            302
/t5-us   /templates/05-neighbourhood/?merchant=corner-crumb   302

# Friendlier aliases for the same two things.
/editorial      /templates/01-editorial-atelier/   302
/counter        /templates/05-neighbourhood/       302
/styleguide     /templates/05-neighbourhood/styleguide.html   302

# The chooser stays at / by design: it shows both directions side by side,
# which is usually the better thing to land a reviewer on.
#
# To make the site open straight on Template 01 instead, uncomment the line
# below. Keep it LAST — these rules are matched top to bottom, and a rule on
# "/" placed earlier would shadow nothing but is clearer at the end.
#
# /   /templates/01-editorial-atelier/   302

# No catch-all splat rule here on purpose. A `/*` rule can shadow static asset
# serving on Cloudflare Pages, which would be a miserable thing to discover
# from a live demo. Both Cloudflare and Netlify serve /404.html automatically
# for unmatched paths, so that file does the job with no rule at all.
